        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "A West Wing of History\r\nFew addresses in South County Dublin carry the weight of history worn so lightly. Kilteragh Pines occupies the site of Kilteragh House, the celebrated mansion built in 1903 by Sir Horace Plunkett - statesman, agricultural reformer, and one of the great architects of Ireland's co-operative movement. Designed in the arts-and-crafts idiom by architect W. H. Caröe, the original house became a legendary gathering place for the leading minds of early twentieth-century Ireland, hosting figures such as George Bernard Shaw, Lady Gregory, W.T. Cosgrave and, only days before his death, Michael Collins himself.\r\n\r\nThough the great house was lost to fire in 1923, its spirit endures. Rebuilt in the following years in the same rambling Edwardian style - gabled rooflines, granite and roughcast walls - the site was reimagined as a select cluster of individual residences, each preserving a piece of Kilteragh's original grandeur. Number 6 forms part of the historic west wing of this remarkable estate.\r\n\r\nOccupying a distinguished position within the west wing of the original house, Number 6 Kilteragh Pines has been tastefully upgraded and modified to provide luxurious accommodation, combining every comfort of modern-day living with the character of its Edwardian origins. Elegant fireplaces and feature high ceilings throughout reflect the bygone era, while the refurbishment ensures a home that is as practical as it is beautiful.\r\n\r\nThe ground floor presents two elegant reception rooms and a dual-aspect kitchen/dining room, complemented by a spacious utility room and guest cloakroom — a layout that balances gracious entertaining space with the practicalities of everyday family life.\r\n\r\nAn elegant staircase rises to the upper floors, where spacious bedrooms are served by recently renovated bathrooms. The main bedroom mirrors the drawing room below, enjoying wonderful proportions and an unrivalled view over the gardens.\r\n\r\nTo the front, residents enjoy an outlook over the majestic communal lawns — the sweeping, mature parkland at the heart of Kilteragh Pines, where yew trees, winding pathways and a clematis-clad pergola create the unmistakable impression of a country estate, just minutes from the city.\r\n\r\nTo the rear, a private wrap-around garden offers a rare degree of seclusion for a home of such character - a sheltered outdoor retreat for entertaining or quiet enjoyment on summer days.\r\n\r\nKilteragh Pines sits within the leafy enclave of Foxrock, one of South Dublin's most sought-after residential addresses, within easy reach of the N11, the Luas at Central Park, and the excellent schools, shops and amenities for which the area is renowned."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "ENTRANCE HALL\r\n5.85m x 2.81m (19'2\" x 9'2\")\r\nFeature high ceilings with recessed lighting detail, dado rail, decorative radiator cover and tiled floor. Understairs storage.\r\n\r\nGUEST CLOAKROOM\r\n2.73m x 1.37m (8'11\" x 4'5\")\r\nWhite suite incorporating a pedestal wash hand basin, wall mirror and wc. Decorative wall panelling, recessed lighting and tiled floor.\r\n\r\nDRAWING ROOM\r\n5.77m x 5.14m (18'11\" x 16'10\")\r\nMajestic fireplace with slate inset and hearth incorporating a coal effect gas fire. Recessed library shelving and decorative radiator covers. Decorative ceiling coving, dado rail and lighting. Picture windows overlooking the gardens.\r\n\r\nFAMILY ROOM\r\n6m x 4.2m (19'8\" x 13'9\")\r\nFeature fireplace with tiled inset incorporating a coal effect gas fire. Concealed pantry storage. Decorative ceiling coving and picture rail. Oak floor and recessed lighting.\r\n\r\nKITCHEN / DINING ROOM\r\n6.26m x 4.95m (20'6\" x 16'2\")\r\nSuperb range of fitted units incorporating De’Bros marble worktop and splashback and a Franke sink. Quality Miele appliances to include a built-in double oven with plate warmer, built-in microwave, a five-ring gas hob, an integrated dishwasher and full-size fridge and freezer. Feature Island ideal for casual dining. Dual aspect room with an abundance of natural light and vaulted light well. Recessed lighting and tiled floor. Door to the garden: -\r\n\r\nUTILITY ROOM\r\n3.66m x 1.56m (12'0\" x 5'1\")\r\nFloor to ceiling fitted units incorporating a stainless-steel sink and drainer and a Miele washing machine and dryer. Tiled floor and recessed lighting.\r\nSTAIRS CASE TO THE FIRST FLOOR\r\n\r\nLANDING\r\nDecorative lighting detail.\r\n\r\nMAIN BEDROOM\r\n5.77m x 5.14m (18'11\" x 16'10\")\r\nPicture windows overlooking the gardens. Decorative radiator covers and ceiling coving.\r\n\r\nBEDROOM 2\r\n4.3m x 3.26m (14'1\" x 10'8\")\r\nDecorative ceiling coving.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nSHOWER ROOM\r\n2.9m x 2.9m (9'6\" x 9'6\")\r\nWhite suite incorporating a shower unit, wash hand basin in vanity unit, illuminated mirror door medicine cabinet and heated towel rail. Tiled walls and floor and recessed lighting. Shelved linen cupboard with an insulated cylinder.\r\n\r\nWC\r\n2.25m x 1.80m (7'4\" x 5'10\")\r\nWhite suite with tiled floor and recessed lighting.\r\n\r\nSTAIRS CASE TO THE SECOND FLOOR\r\n\r\nBEDROOM 3\r\n5.77m x 4.2m (18'11\" x 13'9\")\r\nDecorative radiator cover and recessed lighting.\r\n\r\nSHOWER ROOM\r\n2.09m x 1.73m (6'10\" x 5'8\")\r\nWhite suite incorporating a fully tiled rain spray shower, wash hand basin in vanity unit, wall mirror and wc. Tiled walls and floor.\r\n\r\nBEDROOM 4\r\n3.2m x 3.37m (10'5\" x 11'0\")\r\n\r\nBEDROOM 5 /DRESSING ROOM\r\n4.33m x 2.77m (14'2\" x 9'1\")\r\nWall to wall, floor to ceiling hanging and shelving\r\n\r\nOUTSIDE\r\nThe exacting standards of the interiors have been carried through to the richly stocked landscaped gardens with rolling lawns, mature high hedging and specimen trees, shrubs and herbaceous borders."
      },
